{"type": "FeatureCollection", "features": [{"type": "Feature", "properties": {"name": "Speculative Bristol Airport mass transit route", "speculative": true, "note": "Not a published alignment. WECA's Feb 2026 Transport Vision names Bristol Airport as a mass transit concept, with no route announced. This is Claude's made-up illustration, not a real proposal: from Bristol Temple Meads it follows the Bristol to Taunton railway (OSM way name 'Bristol to Taunton Line') southwest through Bedminster to Bedminster Down Road, where the railway and the A38 run within about 55m of each other. From there it switches to the A38 road corridor (Bristol Road / Bridgwater Road) through Highridge, Bishopsworth, Barrow Gurney and Redhill, staying on the trunk road (still tagged 'Bristol Road' in OSM) past the Downside turn-off to the roundabout where it meets North Side Road, the airport's own one-way access loop, then cuts directly across the roundabout to the terminal building (OSM aeroway=terminal) rather than following the loop's one-way direction \u2014 a new tram alignment is not bound by existing road rules. All of it is traced from OSM except that final ~700m cut, which is a straight-line placeholder."}, "geometry": {"type": "LineString", "coordinates": [[-2.5804029, 51.4490991], [-2.5807482, 51.4490728], [-2.5807516, 51.4489719], [-2.5807526, 51.4489405], [-2.5807582, 51.4487742], [-2.580744, 51.4485686], [-2.5807156, 51.4484134], [-2.5798207, 51.4485112], [-2.5798088, 51.4482997], [-2.5798055, 51.4482267], [-2.5798004, 51.4481369], [-2.5797815, 51.4480266], [-2.5797403, 51.4478266], [-2.5801582, 51.4459668], [-2.5802578, 51.4458123], [-2.5803551, 51.4456927], [-2.5804807, 51.4455552], [-2.5806212, 51.4454239], [-2.5808424, 51.4452454], [-2.5810148, 51.4451274], [-2.5812506, 51.4449907], [-2.581703, 51.4447607], [-2.5821917, 51.4445406], [-2.5826964, 51.4443312], [-2.583312, 51.4440931], [-2.5840494, 51.4438569], [-2.5844968, 51.4437303], [-2.584772, 51.4436578], [-2.5848451,